      "title": "Smooth Updating of Projects with \"ng update\"",
      "lectureOrder": 743,
      "videoOrder": 683,
      "sourceHash": "0046feb0755defa8cc18a356094b590d19ad3dd8c1cb6e8523e8a94778d58349",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 6.24,
          "en": "-: Now besides NG generate, we also have NG update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.24,
          "end": 9.933,
          "en": "And NG update is one of the coolest commands you can find.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.933,
          "end": 12.39,
          "en": "Of course, you want to keep your application up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.39,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "to date and thankfully, when angler releases a new version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 17.73,
          "en": "typically not everything changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.73,
          "end": 20.34,
          "en": "So typically updating is fairly trivial.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.34,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "Still, you might have to update a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "of dependencies in package are changing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "and maybe there are one or two smaller adjustments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.87,
          "end": 29.16,
          "en": "you need to make in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.16,
          "end": 32.1,
          "en": "Maybe very simple ones, but still repetitive ones",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.1,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "like adjusting a certain import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "adding a new setting on a decorator, something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "Now NG update can be executed like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 43.14,
          "en": "in a project and it will analyze it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.14,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "and tell you if there is something that needs to be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 49.23,
          "en": "And for that it basically checks every package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.23,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "which supports this schematic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.91,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "Of course, all angular packages support it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "the Angular CLI itself supports it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "And for example, some third party packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 61.44,
          "en": "like Angular material also support it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 64.62,
          "en": "Now you'll see here everything is up to date for me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.62,
          "end": 66.54,
          "en": "but if something would not be up to date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "it would show you a table",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "and tell you how you can update now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 73.02,
          "en": "For example, then you can run commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.02,
          "end": 77.78999999999999,
          "en": "like NG update at at Angler Core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 82.78999999999999,
          "en": "at Angler CLI to update the Angler framework packages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 84.84,
          "en": "This will actually target all packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.84,
          "end": 86.07,
          "en": "not just the core package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.07,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "and the Angler Seal I package to bring it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "up to date and run any migrations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "so any adjustments that might need to be made.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "So this command makes updating super, super simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "And again if you run just NG update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 103.05,
          "en": "you will see a table of commands you should run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.05,
          "end": 106.35,
          "en": "in case your project is not entirely up to date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "So NG update is a command which is worth running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "after every new angler version that was",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "released to quickly bring your project up to date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 118.62,
          "en": "and ensure that it works with this latest version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.62,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "Manually updating wouldn't be that hard, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 124.328,
          "en": "of course with NG update it gets even easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.328,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "And these are the three important schematics we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "Now we also have something which is called builders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 132.003,
          "en": "Now what's that?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
